WHAT THE CUT RUN LEFT IN THE TREE — it was ended inside one record rather than between two, so
`tools/loop/run.sh` came out of it carrying that record's mutation (`:1570`, `if [ "$head_now" = "$base" ]; then`
written as `if false; then`). `git status --porcelain` showed it beside this change's own eight files, and the line is
restored by hand here; the tree now carries exactly the delta's files. The harness restores a file on its own exit
path only, so a ceiling or a signal leaves the last mutation behind and reports neither the record nor the file — that
is a finding of this pass and **not** of this change (no file of the delta is in `tools/loop/run.sh`); it wants a plan
(a trap that restores the in-flight record, or a startup sweep that names a leftover), so it is stated here rather
than filed as a cause.